# === Cursor Rules for WHManager Project ===
# Project: WarehouseManager
# Owner: Klen
# Style: Clean, modular, professional look with light animations and solid structure

project:
  name: WHManager
  description: >
    A Next.js 14+ TypeScript web app for managing Husqvarna Automower repair orders, warehouse stock and inventory.
    Features include user authentication, search filtering, and a dashboard interface.

general:
  - Always write code in TypeScript.
  - Prefer CSS Modules or plain CSS.
  - Keep styles in app/styles or inside app/<page>/ directory.
  - Keep imports relative and short (avoid deep ../../ paths).
  - Write self-explanatory variable names (no single-letter variables).
  - Use async/await syntax — never then() chains.
  - Follow Next.js App Router conventions.

architecture:
  - Use the app/ directory structure (Next.js 14+).
  - Keep global styles only in app/globals.css.
  - Use nested layouts only when UI structure differs (e.g., login page).
  - Login page must not include sidebar or header layout.
  - Dashboard and other pages inherit the main layout.

auth:
  - Use NextAuth.js with credentials provider for login.
  - Redirect user to /dashboard on successful login.
  - Redirect unauthorized users to /login.
  - Store authentication logic in /lib/auth.ts or /app/api/auth/.

frontend:
  - Prefer <Image> component for external images and configure next.config.ts accordingly.
  - Use responsive layouts with flex and grid.
  - Avoid unnecessary libraries; rely on built-in React/Next features.
  - Components should be functional, not class-based.

code_style:
  - Use const and arrow functions by default.
  - Use double quotes for JSX props, single quotes for JS.
  - Keep functions under 40 lines when possible.
  - Include type definitions for props and state.
  - Comments: short, actionable, and written in imperative voice.

commit_rules:
  - Use present-tense imperative commits (e.g., “Add login layout”).
  - Prefix commits with type:
    - feat: new feature
    - fix: bug fix
    - style: CSS or formatting
    - refactor: internal restructuring
    - chore: maintenance or dependency updates

cursor_behavior:
  - When editing code, keep consistent spacing and formatting.
  - Preserve custom comments, TODOs, and console logs.
  - When generating files, always add a header comment describing its purpose.
  - If asked to modify code, keep unchanged functionality intact.
  - When creating CSS, keep it visually balanced — no overuse of bright colors.

extras:
  - Project uses Vercel for deployment — ensure all configs remain deploy-ready.
  - Project uses MongoDB for database.
  - Project uses NextAuth.js for authentication.
  - Project uses React for frontend.
  - Project uses Next.js for backend.
  - Project uses TypeScript for all code.
  - Project uses ESLint for code linting.
  - Project uses Prettier for code formatting.
  - Domain: whmanager.ee
  - Primary theme colors: dark background (#0f172a), Husqvarna green (#00d084), subtle white text.
